{"name":"Crystal Dark Red","hex":"#6d2c32","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crystal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A solid composed of an array of atoms or molecules possessing long-range order and arranged in a pattern which is periodic in three dimensions.","A piece of glimmering, shining mineral resembling ice or glass."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of crystal.","Very clear; coherent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crystal"},{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maroon","blocks":[{"text":"Maroon is a brownish red color that takes its name from the French word marron, meaning chestnut. Marron is also one of the French translations for \"brown\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg/330px-Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maroon"},{"title":"Crystal","blocks":[{"text":"A crystal or crystalline solid is a solid material whose constituents are arranged in a highly ordered microscopic structure, forming a crystal lattice that extends in all directions. In addition, macroscopic single crystals are usually identifiable by their geometrical shape, consisting of flat faces with specific, characteristic orientations. The scientific study of crystals and crystal formation is known as crystallography. The process of crystal formation via mechanisms of crystal growth is called crystallization or solidification."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Quartz_28.jpg/330px-Quartz_28.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crystal"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg/500px-Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg/500px-Textile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATextile_LACMA_M.55.12.27.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Kiasma_Theatre_%281%29%2C_1998.jpg/500px-Kiasma_Th